<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">351 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">351 CE in world history: 3 events, 1 birth, 1 state founded and 1 that came to an end. 145 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/313">313 CE</a><a href="/years/325">325 CE</a><a href="/years/328">328 CE</a><a href="/years/337">337 CE</a><a href="/years/351" aria-current="page">351 CE</a><a href="/years/357">357 CE</a><a href="/years/363">363 CE</a><a href="/years/378">378 CE</a><a href="/years/392">392 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantius-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-15">15 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Constantius II raises his cousin Gallus to the rank of caesar</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">As he prepared to move against the usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnentius">Magnentius</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a> needed a representative in the East and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Gallus</a> caesar at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirmium">Sirmium</a>, giving him the name Constantius and his sister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirta">Constantina</a> in marriage. Gallus set up residence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnentius">Magnentius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-7">7 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Constantius Gallus arrives at Antioch as Caesar of the East</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Gallus</a>, appointed Caesar by his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirmium">Sirmium</a> in March, reached his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>. Around this time the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> revolted under Isaac of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sepphoris">Diocaesarea</a>, a rising that Gallus's general Ursicinus later put down.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantius-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-28">28 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Constantius II defeats the usurper Magnentius at Mursa</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Mursa, near the Via Militaris in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>, the eastern Roman armies of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a> defeated the western forces of the usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnentius">Magnentius</a>. One of the bloodiest battles in Roman history, it was a pyrrhic victory for Constantius.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnentius">Magnentius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
